{
  "rationale": "No race telemetry exists yet (iteration 0), so this draft is a reasoned first guess rather than a tuned design. Speed: the course is about 4-5 m and must finish in under 3 s, so average speed must reach roughly 1.5 m/s. I set base_speed to 1.8 (about 90% of full PWM) to leave margin for slowdowns in bends without pushing the robot off the 25 mm tape. Geometry: five sensors spaced 15 mm apart across x = -0.03 to +0.03 m, placed 30 mm ahead of the axle so they read the line before the wheels reach it. The 12 mm footprint is narrower than the tape, so the sensors can resolve the line edge and centre. Sensor weights are proportional to lateral position (-2, -1, 0, 1, 2), so a positive signal means the line is on the left and the robot steers left, matching the control convention. Gains: kp = 2.0 gives a moderate steering response (a signal of about 1 produces a 700 PWM differential). ki = 0.1 is small to avoid wind-up on curves. kd = 0.05 is light damping to limit jitter from the sensor noise without over-damping. Line loss uses last_direction so the robot recovers toward the side it was leaving the tape. Wheel track, radius, body and mass are typical mid-range values for stability and traction. Expected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with the slalom the most likely failure point because of its repeated sharp direction changes. Measurements request covers the full set so the next iteration has the data it needs to tune gains and speed.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.03, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": -0.015, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.015, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.03, "y": 0.03}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.8,
    "kp": 2.0,
    "ki": 0.1,
    "kd": 0.05,
    "sensor_weights": [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation",
      "control_effort",
      "controller_errors",
      "noise_robustness"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor draft",
      "notes": "First draft with no prior telemetry: five sensors with proportional weights, moderate kp, light kd, and base_speed 1.8 to meet the 1.5 m/s pace. Expected to complete the oval and s-bend, with the slalom the likely weak point; all metrics requested for tuning."
    }
  }
}
